<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU cocoa, coffee, sugar imports from ACP up in '95.</title>
<headline>EU cocoa, coffee, sugar imports from ACP up in '95.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of European Union imports of coffee and cocoa from African, Caribbean and Pacific (ACP) countries rose by 8.4 and 4.2 percent respectively in 1995 from 1994, Eurostat, the EU's statistical office, said.</p>
<p>The volume of raw sugar cane imports rose by nine percent and bananas by 1.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Soaring world prices meant the value of coffee imports rose by 45.4 percent to reach 1.63 billion European currency units, its latest figures showed.</p>
<p>Main imports were as follows (value in millions of European currency units, volume in thousands of tonnes, changes in percent)-</p>
<p>		    Value    Volume   Value change Volume change</p>
<p> Coffee	   1,629.1	647.5     45.4	   8.4</p>
<p> Cocoa beans    1,091.1	930.1	6.2	   4.2</p>
<p> Raw sugar cane   769.5    1,482.5	7.5	   9.0</p>
<p> Bananas	    406.7	739.5     -7.5	   1.5</p>
<p>-- David Fox, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6832</p>
</text>
